IMPORT prelude

-- Extradition Act 1968 (Singapore) -- when a request from abroad concerns an "extradition offence" (s 2(1), (3)), the bars to
-- surrender to a foreign State and to a declared Commonwealth territory (ss 8, 9, 28), the Minister's duty and discretion to refuse
-- (ss 8(8), 10, 29), and the clocks a person in extradition proceedings meets (ss 15A, 17, 18, 19, 22), with the Malaysian
-- route's offence threshold and discharge clock (ss 32(2), 38).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EA1968.txt, with amendments
-- annotated to Act 15 of 2026 (in force 1 July 2026; a First Schedule entry) shown. Most of the provisions encoded here were
-- substituted by Act 17 of 2022 (wef 1 July 2022) and Act 31 of 2022 (wef 1 November 2022).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the questions a fugitive's counsel
-- meets first: is the offence extraditable, does a bar apply, can the Minister refuse, and what deadlines run. Not encoded: how the
-- Act comes to apply to a State (ss 3-6, 40, 41), warrants and search (ss 11-15), bail (s 14), surrender by consent beyond its
-- clock (s 21), property (s 20), extradition to Singapore (ss 23-26), the Malaysian route beyond ss 32(2), 36 and
-- 38, evidence (ss 42-46), simultaneous requests (s 49), and the First Schedule's list of excluded offences, which turns on the
-- Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 2000 and is taken here as a given fact.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Extradition Act 1968 -- requests`

DECLARE Requester IS ONE OF
    `a foreign State`
    `a declared Commonwealth territory`

-- One request for the surrender of one person for one offence, as the Act's tests see it.
DECLARE Request
    HAS `requester`                                     IS A Requester
        `maximum years abroad`                          IS A NUMBER
        `conduct would be an offence in Singapore`      IS A BOOLEAN
        `maximum years in Singapore`                    IS A NUMBER
        `the Singapore offence is excluded`             IS A BOOLEAN
        `political in character`                        IS A BOOLEAN
        `against a head of state, head of government or minister, or murder` IS A BOOLEAN
        `speciality protection is provided`             IS A BOOLEAN
        `held, on bail or serving a sentence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
        `acquitted, pardoned or punished already`       IS A BOOLEAN
        `convicted in absence`                          IS A BOOLEAN
        `deliberately absent from trial`                IS A BOOLEAN
        `entitled to a retrial in presence`             IS A BOOLEAN
        `time-barred in the requesting place`           IS A BOOLEAN
        `military offence only`                         IS A BOOLEAN
        `Minister believes persecution`                 IS A BOOLEAN
        `Minister satisfied surrender unjust or oppressive` IS A BOOLEAN
        `committed outside both and not extra-territorial there` IS A BOOLEAN
        `immune from prosecution or punishment`         IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `2(1), (3) -- extradition offence`

-- s 2(1) "extradition offence" (b), in relation to a request made by a foreign State or a declared Commonwealth territory: (i) an
-- offence against the law of that State or territory "that carries a maximum punishment of imprisonment for not less than 2 years or
-- any more severe punishment"; and (ii) the act or omission "would, if it took place in or within the jurisdiction of Singapore,
-- constitute an offence against the law in force in Singapore that -- (A) carries a maximum punishment of imprisonment for not less
-- than 2 years or any more severe punishment; and (B) is not an excluded offence".
-- s 2(3): an offence is not prevented from being an extradition offence "merely because it is an offence of a purely fiscal
-- character" -- so there is no fiscal flag here at all.
-- The "more severe punishment" limb (eg death) is not modelled; give it as a long maximum in years.
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is an extradition offence` IF
        `the request`'s `maximum years abroad` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the request`'s `conduct would be an offence in Singapore`
    AND `the request`'s `maximum years in Singapore` AT LEAST 2
    AND (NOT `the request`'s `the Singapore offence is excluded`)

§§ `8(1), 9(1), 28 -- offences of a political character`

-- ss 8(1), 9(1): not liable to be surrendered if the offence "is an offence of a political character" or is one "by reason of the
-- circumstances". s 28(1): "For the purposes of section 9(1)" -- declared Commonwealth territories only -- an offence against the
-- life or person of a head of state or of his or her immediate family, of a head of government or a minister, murder, and
-- accessory, attempt and conspiracy offences to these, "are not offences of a political character". s 8 has no such list.
-- (s 28(2) lets the Minister restrict the list by order for a territory with similar laws; not modelled.)
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the political-offence bar applies` IF
        `the request`'s `political in character`
    AND CONSIDER `the request`'s `requester`
        WHEN `a foreign State` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a declared Commonwealth territory` THEN NOT `the request`'s `against a head of state, head of government or minister, or murder`

§§ `8(5), (6) -- bars that apply to a foreign State only`

-- s 8(5): not liable if "convicted of that offence in the foreign State in his or her absence, unless -- (a) the person had
-- deliberately absented himself or herself ...; or (b) the person would, if surrendered, be entitled to a retrial in his or her
-- presence". s 8(6): not liable if prosecution is "barred by the passage of time" under the foreign State's law.
-- s 9 has neither. For a declared Commonwealth territory the same facts are only grounds on which the Minister "may decline" (s 29).
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the in-absence conviction bar applies` IF
        `the request`'s `convicted in absence`
    AND (NOT `the request`'s `deliberately absent from trial`)
    AND (NOT `the request`'s `entitled to a retrial in presence`)

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a foreign-State-only bar applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the request`'s `requester`
    WHEN `a foreign State` THEN
            `the in-absence conviction bar applies` `the request`
        OR  `the request`'s `time-barred in the requesting place`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `8 and 9 -- not liable to be surrendered`

-- ss 8(2), 9(2): not liable "unless provision is made" (by law, treaty, or for a territory an agreement or undertaking) that the
-- person will not be detained or tried for other earlier offences, or re-surrendered elsewhere ("speciality").
-- ss 8(3), 9(3): not liable while "held in custody, or ... released on bail, in Singapore in respect of an offence that is alleged to
-- have been committed in Singapore" or "undergoing a sentence for a conviction in Singapore", until discharged.
-- ss 8(4), 9(4): not liable if "acquitted or pardoned" or has "undergone the punishment" in any state or territory for that offence
-- or another constituted by the same act or omission.
-- ss 8(7), 9(5): not liable if the conduct would be an offence "under the military law applicable in Singapore but not also under
-- the ordinary criminal law of Singapore".
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a bar to surrender applies` IF
        `the political-offence bar applies` `the request`
    OR  (NOT `the request`'s `speciality protection is provided`)
    OR  `the request`'s `held, on bail or serving a sentence in Singapore`
    OR  `the request`'s `acquitted, pardoned or punished already`
    OR  `the request`'s `military offence only`
    OR  `a foreign-State-only bar applies` `the request`

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is liable to be surrendered` IF
        `the offence is an extradition offence` `the request`
    AND (NOT `a bar to surrender applies` `the request`)

§§ `10, 21(7) -- the Minister must refuse`

-- s 10(1): the Minister "must not" give a notice under s 11(1) or issue a surrender warrant if "the Minister has substantial grounds
-- for believing" that the request was made to prosecute or punish the person "on account of his or her race, religion, sex, ethnic
-- origin, nationality or political opinions", or that the person may be prejudiced at trial or punished for those reasons.
-- s 10(2): nor if, by reason of triviality, bad faith, "the passage of time" or "any other sufficient cause", "it would be unjust,
-- oppressive or too severe a punishment to surrender the fugitive".
-- s 21(7) (surrender by consent): "if any of the restrictions on surrender in those sections [8, 9 and 10] are applicable, the
-- Minister is not to issue a warrant of surrender".
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must refuse under section 10` IF
        `the request`'s `Minister believes persecution`
    OR  `the request`'s `Minister satisfied surrender unjust or oppressive`

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may order surrender` IF
        `the person is liable to be surrendered` `the request`
    AND (NOT `the Minister must refuse under section 10` `the request`)

§§ `29 -- declared Commonwealth territories: the Minister may decline`

-- s 29: the Minister "may decline" for a fugitive from a declared Commonwealth territory if (a) the judgment was rendered in his or
-- her absence (same two exceptions as s 8(5)); (b) the offence "was committed outside Singapore and the declared Commonwealth
-- territory" and "is not an extra-territorial offence" under that territory's law; or (c) the fugitive has "become immune from
-- prosecution or punishment because of any reason, including lapse of time or amnesty".
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may decline under section 29` IF
    CONSIDER `the request`'s `requester`
    WHEN `a declared Commonwealth territory` THEN
            `the in-absence conviction bar applies` `the request`
        OR  `the request`'s `committed outside both and not extra-territorial there`
        OR  `the request`'s `immune from prosecution or punishment`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `8(8) -- short remaining sentences, foreign States`

-- s 8(8): where a foreign State asks for surrender to enforce a sentence on a convicted fugitive, the Minister "may determine that
-- the person is not to be surrendered" if the remaining period "(a) is shorter than the period specified as being a minimal period
-- in the provisions of any existing extradition treaty ...; or (b) is less than 6 months, if no period mentioned in paragraph (a) is
-- specified". Months in, a discretion out; s 8(8) names only foreign States.
GIVEN `requester` IS A Requester, `months remaining` IS A NUMBER, `the treaty specifies a minimal period` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `treaty minimal months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may refuse for a short remaining sentence` IF
    CONSIDER `requester`
    WHEN `a foreign State` THEN
        IF `the treaty specifies a minimal period`
        THEN `months remaining` < `treaty minimal months`
        ELSE `months remaining` < 6
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `15A, 17, 18, 19 -- clocks in the Magistrate's and the High Court's proceedings`

-- s 15A(2): the Magistrate may remand "for a period or periods not exceeding 7 days at any one time".
GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remand period is within section 15A` IF
    `days` AT MOST 7

-- s 17(4)(b): notice of an application for review of the Magistrate's order "must be filed with the Registrar of the State Courts
-- not later than 15 days after the order is made".
GIVEN `days after the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the review notice is in time` IF
    `days after the order` AT MOST 15

-- s 18(3)(a): an application for permission to refer, or the Attorney-General's reference, of a question of law of public interest
-- to the Court of Appeal "must be made within 15 days, or any longer period as the Court of Appeal may permit".
GIVEN `days after the determination` IS A NUMBER, `the Court of Appeal permitted longer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference to the Court of Appeal is in time` IF
        `days after the determination` AT MOST 15
    OR  `the Court of Appeal permitted longer`

-- s 18(1), (2): a party needs the Court of Appeal's permission; "The Attorney-General may refer ... without the permission".
GIVEN `the party is the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permission to refer is needed` IF
    NOT `the party is the Attorney-General`

-- s 19(1)(b), (2): the prisoner "will not be surrendered until after the expiry of the period of 15 days after the date of the
-- committal or order, unless the prisoner waives" the right to review; the Minister's warrant comes after the later of that expiry
-- and the High Court's final determination of any review. s 19(5), (8): on a recorded waiver the Minister may issue the warrant
-- "after the date of the recording of the consent". The "after the expiry" is read as from day 16.
GIVEN `days since committal` IS A NUMBER, `waiver recorded` IS A BOOLEAN, `review pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may now issue a surrender warrant` IF
    IF `waiver recorded`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `days since committal` > 15 AND (NOT `review pending`)

§§ `22, 32(2), 36, 38 -- discharge if not conveyed out, and the Malaysian route`

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `Part 3 -- a foreign State or declared Commonwealth territory`
    `Part 6 -- Malaysia`

-- s 22(1): a person committed and "in custody in Singapore at the expiry of 2 months after the latest of" committal, the High
-- Court's final determination of a review, or the Court of Appeal's on a reference "may apply ... to be released"; (2) the court "is
-- to order that the person be released" on proof of reasonable notice to the Minister; (3) not "if reasonable cause is shown for the
-- delay". s 38 (Malaysia): the same, but "at the expiration of one month", with notice to the person holding him or her in custody.
GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the discharge period in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `Part 3 -- a foreign State or declared Commonwealth territory` THEN 2
    WHEN `Part 6 -- Malaysia` THEN 1

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route, `months since the latest date` IS A NUMBER, `reasonable notice given` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonable cause for delay shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the High Court must order release` IF
        `months since the latest date` AT LEAST `the discharge period in months` `the route`
    AND `reasonable notice given`
    AND (NOT `reasonable cause for delay shown`)

-- s 32(2): in Part 6 "offence" means "an arrestable offence or an offence punishable on conviction with imprisonment for 6 months or
-- more or any more severe punishment under the law of Malaysia". Part 6 does not use "extradition offence"; whether s 2(1)'s
-- double-criminality test also reaches Malaysian requests is not something the text of Part 6 says (inference: it does not).
GIVEN `arrestable under Malaysian law` IS A BOOLEAN, `maximum months in Malaysia` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is within Part 6` IF
        `arrestable under Malaysian law`
    OR  `maximum months in Malaysia` AT LEAST 6

-- s 36: the Magistrate "may" release, defer surrender or make another order where, by reason of triviality, bad faith or "the passage
-- of time", "it would be unjust, oppressive or too severe a punishment to surrender the person to Malaysia". Under s 10(2) the same
-- finding binds the Minister ("must not"); under s 36 it leaves the Magistrate a choice.
GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an unjust-or-oppressive finding compels refusal` IF
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `Part 3 -- a foreign State or declared Commonwealth territory` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 6 -- Malaysia` THEN FALSE
